# Firma Integration Rules

## Status Inference — Do Not Rely on Firma's Aggregate Status Alone

Firma keeps its top-level `status` field as `"pending"` or `"in_progress"` until **every** signer completes. A partial signature never advances the aggregate status.

Always infer our internal status from per-signer `signed_at` counts **in addition to** the aggregate status field:

```typescript
// After merging firmaUsers into updatedSigners:
const signedCount = updatedSigners.filter(s => s.signed_at).length;
const signerCount = updatedSigners.length;

if (signerCount > 0 && signedCount === signerCount) {
  newStatus = "completed";  // all signed
} else if (signedCount > 0 && statusPriority[newStatus] < statusPriority["viewed"]) {
  newStatus = "viewed";     // partial signing
}
```

## mapFirmaStatus — Always Normalise Before Switching

Firma has used different status strings across API versions. Always normalise before comparing:

```typescript
const s = raw.toLowerCase().replace(/[\s_\-]+/g, "_");
// covers: completed, complete, signed, fully_signed, executed, done, finished
// covers: pending, in_progress, active, awaiting, open, processing → "sent"
```

## Response Shape — Never Assume a Single Nesting Depth

Firma may return `{ id, status }` flat **or** `{ data: { id, status } }` **or** `{ signing_request: { id, status } }`. Always use `extractField()`:

```typescript
function extractField(raw: Record<string, unknown>, key: string): string | null {
  if (typeof raw[key] === "string") return raw[key] as string;
  for (const w of ["data", "signing_request", "result", "record"]) {
    const val = (raw[w] as Record<string, unknown> | undefined)?.[key];
    if (typeof val === "string") return val;
  }
  return null;
}
```

## Workspace Key — Always Fall Back to Master Key on 401/403

The cached workspace key in `firma_workspaces` can become stale. Any Firma API call that receives 401/403 must retry with `process.env.FIRMA_API_KEY`:

```typescript
let res = await fetch(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${workspaceKey}` } });
if ((res.status === 401 || res.status === 403) && process.env.FIRMA_API_KEY) {
  res = await fetch(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.FIRMA_API_KEY}` } });
}
```

## Webhook Timestamp Tolerance

Firma re-uses the **original** HMAC timestamp on retries. Tolerance must be ≥ 1 hour (3600 s) or retries will be silently rejected.

## Vercel Logs — Last Line Only

Vercel's per-request log view shows only the **last** `console.log` line. Put a single comprehensive summary log at the very end of each route handler:

```typescript
console.log(`[sync-status] ✅ done | db: "${oldStatus}" → "${newStatus}" | signers: ${signedCount}/${signerCount} | changed: ${hasChanges}`);
```

## Never Throw in getFirmaSigningRequestById

An unexpected response shape must return `null`, never throw. Throws are silently caught upstream and leave the DB status unchanged with no visible error.
